  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Calculate the number of radial nodes using the</p><p>Number of radial nodes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8467;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>Radial nodes= number of cuts on x-axis ( r).<br />The curve should start from zero. It can be positive or negative.<br />Size of the curve increases after touching the x- axis every time&nbsp;.</p><p>By keeping all this, we get the following curve:<br />&nbsp;</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/744dce1f-2f78-4ee6-8036-bda308900642-image.png\" style=\"width: 286px; height: 185px;\" /></p><p>Therefor corresponding graph is (C)</p><p>Hence, answer is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p>",
